From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:26 +0200
Subject: dt-bindings: rtc: allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc: add the external 32k
 crystal

The A10/A20 RTC can run its 32 kHz low-speed oscillator (LOSC) either
from an internal RC oscillator or from an external 32.768 kHz crystal.
Besides the RTC itself, LOSC is the clock behind the CLK_OUT_A/B pins,
which boards use as the low-power clock (LPO) of their WiFi/Bluetooth
module.

Add an optional clocks property describing the crystal, similar to the
A31 RTC binding.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rtc/allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rtc/allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rtc/allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rtc/allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/rtc/allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc.yaml
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@ properties:
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      External 32.768 kHz crystal. When present, the RTC selects it as
+      the source of its low-speed oscillator (LOSC) instead of the
+      internal RC oscillator. Only describe it on boards that have the
+      crystal fitted.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
@@ -38,6 +46,7 @@ examples:
         compatible = "allwinner,sun4i-a10-rtc";
         reg = <0x01c20d00 0x20>;
         interrupts = <24>;
+        clocks = <&ext_osc32k>;
     };
 
 ...
